        "source_sha256": "1b2adcddc2401827486b996d4d23eecb07c1d15bd2a2c535b2604fcdf6d43c08",
        "text": "- Home\n- Meet Jason\n- Issues\n- Endorsements\n- Contact\n# Join Our Campaign\nSign up to receive the latest news and updates.\nFirst name Email Zip/Postal Phone Message\nBy providing your phone number you consent to receive messages. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Text STOP to opt out.\nThank you for signing up!\n# Why I’m Running\nEvery family and business in Alameda County Water District (ACWD), Ward 2 deserves to know that their water supply will not be affected. As an experienced engineer for a different water district, Jason is ready to serve you on Day 1. ACWD Ward 2 is ready for leadership that reflects that. Wasteful water usage should be stopped so that your water rates stay low and affordable. With AI usage increasing, data centers are being proposed throughout the state. These data centers use heavy amounts of water. ACWD should implement strict water consumption monitoring reports if these data centers cannot use recycled water. ACWD should collaborate with the Tri-Cities to ensure your water supply is safeguarded in the long-term.\nThere is a lack of opportunity for you to serve on boards and commissions at ACWD. You should have the opportunity to ensure that your monthly bills are being spent wisely. A youth commission should be established so that future generations can learn about the government process and help steer ACWD to support long-term growth.\n# What Does ACWD Do For You?\nMany of you wonder what is the Alameda County Water District (ACWD) and how does it affect you. In short, ACWD supplies the residents and businesses in the Tri-City Area (Newark, Fremont, and Union City) water. When you turn on the faucet, water comes out. ACWD is responsible in ensuring that the water supply continues to flow to you when you turn on the faucet or shower. ACWD owns pipelines and treatment plants that supply you with water.\nRecently, ACWD has adopted district based elections to ensure each area in within the Tri-City Area is represented. If you live in the City of Newark and in portions of Fremont (west of I-880), you live in Ward 2.\n### Register to Vote Below\nIf you are 18 years old or over and are not registered to vote, please click the here to register. If you are between the ages of 16-18 you can also pre-register to vote by clicking the button below and you are automatically registered to vote when you turn 18.\n### Election Day\nNovember 3, 2026 at 8:00 AM\n- Issues\n- Endorsements\n- Contact\nJason Miguel For ACWD, Ward 2\nPowered by CampaignPartner.com\n- Home\n- Meet Jason\n- Issues\n- Endorsements\n- Contact\nClose Menu",
        "text_limited": false,
        "title": "Jason Miguel for ACWD, Ward 2",
        "unresolved_images": []
